+/*
+** STONE: Reset request-scoped cookie state to its initial values.
+**
+** The aParam[] entries point into the per-request zCookieValue buffer (and into
+** transient query-parameter strings), all of which are freed when the request's
+** db/cgi state is torn down. cookie_parse() short-circuits on bIsInit and never
+** rezeroes nParam, so in the embedded in-process server (repeated fossil_main()
+** calls; see scripts/fossil-inprocess.patch) the next request would dereference
+** those dangling pointers and crash. Clearing the whole struct forces a fresh
+** parse each request. Called from the HTTP request entry point.
+*/
+void cookie_reset_state(void){
+  memset(&cookies, 0, sizeof(cookies));
+}
