+** manifest_crosslink_end() and leaves it set, so the *next* invocation's
+** manifest_crosslink_begin() trips the assert. seenManifests (a has-seen
+** cache its own comment above says is freed "only from the app's atexit()
+** handler") and manifest_event_triggers_are_enabled (guarding a
+** `temp.alert_trigger1` TEMP TRIGGER that db_close() drops at the end of
+** *every* invocation, success or not) have the same problem: both describe
+** state tied to one SQLite connection but outlive it as plain C statics.
+** Called from the top of every fossil_main() (see src/main.c), not just
+** after an abort -- a normal invocation should already have these at these
+** values, so resetting unconditionally is always safe and needs no path
+** tracking.
+*/
+void manifest_reset_state(void){
+  manifest_crosslink_busy = 0;
+  manifest_event_triggers_are_enabled = 0;
+  bag_clear(&seenManifests);
+}
